one to lose weight well have a huge bowl  of salad most of us think that by having  salad on a daily basis it can help with  weight loss that is true a huge bowl of  salad contains all the nutrients  vitamins and minerals that your body  needs plus it is very hard to overeat  but what you choose to dress your salad  with can be a killer it can turn a  really healthy meal into a calorie bomb  I'm talking about store-bought salad  dressings which are very high in fat  salt sugar and even additives each  tablespoon has about 70 to 100 calories  this a sneaky calories and they are  probably ruining your diet without you  even realizing it you must be thinking  my salad must be really tasteless and  boring hey make your own salad dressings  instead they are cheap easy to make  healthy and you can control what you put  in it so here are four of my favorite  low-fat salad dressings for a lighter  version always up for vinaigrette based  dressing so my first recipe is the spicy  lime vinaigrette dressing what you'll  need are three tablespoons of lemon  juice three tablespoons of rice wine  vinegar one tablespoon of light soy  sauce half a tablespoon of sesame oil  half a tablespoon of extra virgin olive  oil half a tablespoon of maple syrup one  garlic clove minced and half a teaspoon  of dried chili flakes mix all the  ingredients in a bowl and stir until  well combined  each tablespoon has about 23 calories  drizzle a couple of tablespoons onto  your salad and serve do you know that  one tablespoon of ranch dressing has  about 73 calories the recipe usually  calls for mayonnaise sour cream and  buttermilk for healthy twist we're going  to replace the cream with silken tofu  don't worry guys you will barely taste  the tofu this recipe has under 10  calories per tablespoon it is still  thick creamy and packed with herbs and  spices what you'll need are one cup  of silken tofu 1 tablespoon of lemon  juice quarter teaspoon of garlic powder  quarter teaspoon of dried chives quarter  teaspoon of dried mixed herbs quarter  teaspoon of cayenne pepper and salt and  pepper to taste simply blend the silken  tofu in a blender until smooth then mix  all the ingredients in a bowl and stir  until well combined  well if tofu is not your thing then just  replace it with yogurt who loves as it  key also known as Greek cucumber yogurt  here's a really simple recipe you can  follow so what I've used are half a cup  of yogurt 1/2 a cup of cucumber finely  grated cut a cup of mint leaves finely  chopped 2 teaspoons of lemon juice 1  garlic clove minced and a pinch of salt  and pepper again simply mix all the  ingredients in a bowl you can choose to  chill in the fridge before serving each  quarter cup only has about 28 calories  it's refreshing creamy and zingy I like  to dip it with some chopped up  vegetables such as cucumbers carrots and  even celery or you can choose to serve  it with some bread and even grilled meat  if you love Tomatoes try this final  recipe to mutter vinaigrette what you'll  need are have a can of diced tomatoes  cut a cup of shallots diced 1 garlic  clove minced one-and-a-half tablespoons  of apple cider vinegar 2 tablespoons of  extra-virgin olive oil a pinch of  cayenne pepper and a pinch of salt and  pepper  in a bowl add all the ingredients mix  well and serve each tablespoon has about  21 calories this flavorful tomato  vinaigrette is not only great with salad  it is also delicious with roasted  vegetables grilled meat seafood or serve  it as a dip the next time you enjoy a  bowl of salad just be really aware of  the dressing choose to serve it on the  side and enjoy in small quantities or  make your own instead so try all these  recipes out and let me know which is  your favorite in the comments below tag  at Joanna's are official and hashtag  chaser recipes guys like this video  share this video and subscribe to my  youtube channel for a lot more healthy  recipes workout videos and also fitness  tips do turn on your notification button  so that you will get notified every time  I share a new video all the best
 

